all_claims:
The electronic device (150, 1400) of one of claims 1 to 9, further comprising:
 a bit stream memory access unit, BSMAU (208), and a header memory access unit, HMAU (209), wherein the BSMAU (208) is configured to cause encoded data in the combined data stream to be stored in a buffer (706, 714) at a first memory location, and wherein the HMAU is configured to cause slice information (1304) from the encoding to be stored in a second memory location relative to the first memory location; 
 wherein the slice information (1304) is contained in a slice index table.

The electronic device (150, 1400) of claim 10, wherein the BSMAU (208) includes a slice header formation module (704) configured to identify slice header information, and wherein for a slice (420, 422, 424), the slice header information includes at least one of:
 a slice header size; 
 a scale factor (812); 
 a size of luma data in the slice (420, 422, 424); and 
 a size of chroma data in the slice (420, 422, 424).

The electronic device (150, 1400) of claim 11, wherein the slice header information for the slice (420, 422, 424) is stored in the buffer (706, 714) along with the encoded data in the combined data stream of the slice (420, 422, 424) when the buffer (706, 714) is sufficient to accommodate both of the slice header information and the encoded data of the slice (420, 422, 424); 
wherein the slice header information for the slice (420, 422, 424) is output to an external storage (210) when the buffer (706, 714) is insufficient to accommodate both of the slice (420, 422, 424) header information and the encoded data of the slice (420, 422, 424); and 
wherein the stored data in the buffer (706, 714) is transmitted to the external storage (210) when a predetermined condition is met.
